Clipboard with boxes (round 13): a copied range holding a square root, fraction or power box goes on the
clipboard as its linear text (for other programs) and as the box flavour (its canonical box text, 4.4); pasting the
box flavour into a code cell inserts the boxes (a plain cell takes its first boxes, its characters stay characters),
at an insertion point it makes one Input cell holding them. Text from other programs stays text, `((` included.
`--- clip` gives the clipboard at the end.

=== a fraction copied from one cell pastes as a fraction into a plain cell
--- before
#% cell typeset
((a)/(b))▮

#% cell
x+
--- keys
Ctrl+A Ctrl+C Click(1,2) Ctrl+V
--- after
#% cell typeset
((a)/(b))

#% cell typeset
x+((a)/(b))▮
--- boxes
x+(a/b)▮
--- clip
text "a/b"
boxes "((a)/(b))"

=== the plain cell's own characters stay characters when it takes the pasted boxes
--- before
#% cell typeset
((a)/(b))▮

#% cell
f((y))+
--- keys
Ctrl+A Ctrl+C Click(1,7) Ctrl+V
--- after
#% cell typeset
((a)/(b))

#% cell typeset
f((y))+((a)/(b))▮
--- boxes
f((y))+(a/b)▮

=== a root pasted into the middle of a fraction's numerator nests there
--- before
#% cell typeset
((sqrt(x)))▮

#% cell typeset
((ab)/(c))
--- keys
Ctrl+A Ctrl+C Click(1,3) Ctrl+V
--- after
#% cell typeset
((sqrt(x)))

#% cell typeset
((a*((sqrt(x)))▮*b)/(c))
--- boxes
(a*√(x)▮*b/c)

=== a part of a slot holding a box copies with it; a slot's plain part copies as text only
--- before
#% cell typeset
((1+((x)^(2)))/(c))▮
--- keys
Ctrl+A Ctrl+C
--- clip
text "(1+x^2)/c"
boxes "((1+((x)^(2)))/(c))"

=== a selection without boxes in a cell with boxes copies as text only
--- before
#% cell typeset
ab+((x)^(2))▮
--- keys
Home Shift+Right Shift+Right Ctrl+C
--- clip
text "ab"

=== Copy as plain text writes the linear text only
--- before
#% cell typeset
((sqrt(x)))▮
--- keys
Ctrl+A Ctrl+Shift+C
--- clip
text "sqrt(x)"

=== a power cut from one cell pastes into another; the cell it left is plain again
--- before
#% cell typeset
y+((x)^(2))▮

#% cell
z
--- keys
Shift+Left Ctrl+X Click(1,1) Ctrl+V
--- after
#% cell
y+

#% cell typeset
z*((x)^(2))▮
--- clip
text "x^2"
boxes "((x)^(2))"

=== pasted boxes replace a selection in a plain cell
--- before
#% cell typeset
((a)/(b))▮

#% cell
1 + abc + 2
--- keys
Ctrl+A Ctrl+C Click(1,4) Shift+Click(1,7) Ctrl+V
--- after
#% cell typeset
((a)/(b))

#% cell typeset
1 + ((a)/(b))▮ + 2
--- boxes
1 + (a/b)▮ + 2

=== pasted boxes replace a selection in a cell with boxes
--- before
#% cell typeset
((sqrt(x)))▮

#% cell typeset
((x)^(2))+1
--- keys
Ctrl+A Ctrl+C Click(1,0) Shift+Right Ctrl+V
--- after
#% cell typeset
((sqrt(x)))

#% cell typeset
((sqrt(x)))▮+1
--- boxes
√(x)▮+1

=== boxes pasted at an insertion point make one Input cell holding them
--- before
#% cell typeset
((x)^(2))▮

#% cell
y
--- keys
Ctrl+A Ctrl+C Gap(2) Ctrl+V
--- after
#% cell typeset
((x)^(2))

#% cell
y

#% cell typeset
((x)^(2))▮
--- boxes
(x^2)▮

=== pasting boxes is one undo unit; undo leaves the plain cell as it was
--- before
#% cell typeset
((a)/(b))▮

#% cell
x+
--- keys
Ctrl+A Ctrl+C Click(1,2) Ctrl+V Ctrl+Z
--- after
#% cell typeset
((a)/(b))

#% cell
x+▮

=== text from another program stays text in a plain cell, `((` included
--- before
#% cell
y = ▮
--- keys
Clip("((a)/(b))") Ctrl+V
--- after
#% cell
y = ((a)/(b))▮
--- boxes
none

=== text from another program stays text in a cell with boxes, `((` included
--- before
#% cell typeset
((x)^(2))▮
--- keys
Clip("+((a)/(b))") Ctrl+V
--- boxes
(x^2)+((a)/(b))▮

=== boxes pasted into a Text cell give their linear text
--- before
#% cell typeset
((a)/(b))▮

#% text
see:
--- keys
Ctrl+A Ctrl+C Click(1,4) Ctrl+V
--- after
#% cell typeset
((a)/(b))

#% text
see:a/b▮

=== copied cells give the linear text of their boxes and the cells flavour
--- before
#% cell typeset ◆
((a)/(b))+1
--- keys
Ctrl+C
--- clip
text "a/b+1"
cells

=== a root copied from typeset output pastes as a root box
--- before
#% cell label=1
2^(1/2)
#% output n=1
#= ⟦2^(1/2)⟧

#% cell
r=
--- keys
TypesetOutputs Ctrl+C Click(2,2) Ctrl+V
--- after
#% cell label=1
2^(1/2)
#% output n=1
#= 2^(1/2)

#% cell typeset
r=((sqrt(2)))▮
--- clip
text "2^(1/2)"
boxes "((sqrt(2)))"

=== a part of typeset output without boxes copies as text only
--- before
#% cell label=1
x + y
#% output n=1
#= ⟦x⟧ + y
--- keys
TypesetOutputs Ctrl+C
--- clip
text "x"
